WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.453
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:04.453 --> 00:00:06.870
Today we're going to talk
about, how to reinvent yourself.

00:00:07.831 --> 00:00:09.499
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:11.150
and make sure to stick around

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.142
all the way to the end, for
some special bonus clips.

00:00:13.142 --> 00:00:14.048
Also, as people are talking,

00:00:14.048 --> 00:00:15.582
if they say something that

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.639
really, really resonates with you,

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:18.406
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:18.406 --> 00:00:19.565
and put quotes around it,

00:00:19.565 --> 00:00:21.921
so other people can be inspired, as well.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.191
Enjoy.

00:00:23.191 --> 00:00:25.774
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.332 --> 00:00:31.915
(bright music)

00:00:40.109 --> 00:00:42.306
- You have to reinvent yourself.

00:00:42.306 --> 00:00:43.935
If the person you are today,

00:00:43.935 --> 00:00:47.040
is not allowing you to get
to where you want to get to,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.282
you don't cry about it,

00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:49.890
you don't whine about it,

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:50.943
you don't waste energy,

00:00:50.943 --> 00:00:52.629
cuz you only have so much of it.

00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:53.462
What you do is say,

00:00:53.462 --> 00:00:55.354
I've got as much as I can get

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:56.413
with what I have.

00:00:56.413 --> 00:00:58.639
I've got as far as I can go,

00:00:58.639 --> 00:01:01.395
with who I am and who I currently am,

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:03.040
is not gon' take me to where I got to be.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.790
So I got to reinvent myself.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.375
So you say, Eric, what do you mean

00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:08.174
when you say reinvent yourself?

00:01:08.174 --> 00:01:10.225
I mean Michael Jordan.

00:01:10.225 --> 00:01:11.058
That's right.

00:01:11.058 --> 00:01:12.715
I know you thought Michael
Jordan won championships

00:01:12.715 --> 00:01:13.997
his first year in the league,

00:01:13.997 --> 00:01:16.043
maybe you thought he won
a championship in second.

00:01:16.043 --> 00:01:16.876
But, no, no, no.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.110
It took Mike, seven years, right.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.036
Seven years to make that
dream become a reality.

00:01:22.036 --> 00:01:23.063
So the first Mike,

00:01:23.063 --> 00:01:24.613
yup, he put up a lot of points.

00:01:24.613 --> 00:01:25.617
Yup, the first Mike,

00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:27.631
he won a dunk contest, you're right.

00:01:27.631 --> 00:01:29.045
Yup, the first Mike put up,

00:01:29.045 --> 00:01:32.750
like 62 against Boston, in
the playoffs and still lost.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:33.583
That's right.

00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:35.266
The Michael Jordan I'm talkin' about

00:01:35.266 --> 00:01:36.782
he had the fresh gym shoes,

00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:37.708
the Nike Airs,

00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:39.185
he had the t-shirts, right.

00:01:39.185 --> 00:01:41.244
Everybody knew him.

00:01:41.244 --> 00:01:43.461
But guess what, that Michael Jordan

00:01:43.461 --> 00:01:46.321
didn't win any championships.

00:01:46.321 --> 00:01:47.364
I'm going to say it again.

00:01:47.364 --> 00:01:49.034
The Mike that could score 62,

00:01:49.034 --> 00:01:51.124
the Mike that could dunk from half court,

00:01:51.124 --> 00:01:53.915
the Mike that could wow
you in the All-Star game.

00:01:53.915 --> 00:01:56.989
The Mike that we all loved.

00:01:56.989 --> 00:01:59.040
That Michael Jordan didn't
win one championship.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.847
And so guess what Mike had to do.

00:02:00.847 --> 00:02:02.980
Mike had to reinvent himself.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.446
And so what did he do?

00:02:04.446 --> 00:02:06.196
Mike started playing both ways.

00:02:06.196 --> 00:02:08.923
He just didn't play offense
no more, he played defense.

00:02:08.923 --> 00:02:11.404
He didn't score a lot,
but he started to pass.

00:02:11.404 --> 00:02:13.499
He started to work out a little different.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:14.852
He developed not just a dunk,

00:02:14.852 --> 00:02:17.204
but he developed a little 16 foot eject,

00:02:17.204 --> 00:02:19.319
you know the little fade away.

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:20.204
And guess what?

00:02:20.204 --> 00:02:22.214
The new Mike, ditched the old Mike.

00:02:22.214 --> 00:02:23.384
He just said, well ya know what,

00:02:23.384 --> 00:02:25.712
I'm puttin' up 62, I'm
gettin' discouraged.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.743
You know what I'm sayin'.

00:02:26.743 --> 00:02:29.259
I'm doin' all kinds of
shootin', I'm scorin',

00:02:29.259 --> 00:02:31.182
I'm winnin' titles, I'm
winnin' championships.

00:02:31.182 --> 00:02:33.324
No, no, no, no, no he didn't say that.

00:02:33.324 --> 00:02:34.919
He says, I'm not able to do that,

00:02:34.919 --> 00:02:36.869
because the man I am, is not takin'

00:02:36.869 --> 00:02:38.925
me to that point, and so
I got to reinvent myself.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.270
And so he didn't give up, he didn't quit.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:42.429
He reinvented himself.

00:02:42.429 --> 00:02:44.397
He started playin' defense, baby.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.135
He started passin', baby.

00:02:46.135 --> 00:02:49.387
He started shootin' instead of
just dunkin' and guess what?

00:02:49.387 --> 00:02:52.031
He went from one, to two, to three,

00:02:52.031 --> 00:02:55.262
to four, to five, to six championships.

00:02:55.262 --> 00:02:57.384
And many of us believe,
had he not retired,

00:02:57.384 --> 00:03:00.600
he probably would have won eight
titles, baby, that's right.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.092
Diaper Dandy, baby.

00:03:02.092 --> 00:03:03.048
Eight titles.

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:05.345
And so it's your boy ET sayin' number one,

00:03:05.345 --> 00:03:08.266
you got to reinvent yourself,

00:03:08.266 --> 00:03:09.099
right?

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:11.962
If you're not where you want to
be, don't quit, don't give up.

00:03:11.962 --> 00:03:14.558
If you're not getting
the goals accomplished,

00:03:14.558 --> 00:03:16.406
if you're not making your dream come--

00:03:16.406 --> 00:03:18.891
don't quit, reinvent yourself.

00:03:18.891 --> 00:03:22.762
- Entrepreneurs who have
authored a product or a process

00:03:22.762 --> 00:03:24.637
that isn't working today,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.477
have to make the bold step

00:03:26.477 --> 00:03:28.644
of reinventing themselves.

00:03:29.645 --> 00:03:31.110
I talk about it all the time.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.843
How over the course of my life,

00:03:32.843 --> 00:03:34.151
whether it was at 12 years old,

00:03:34.151 --> 00:03:37.074
or 18 years old, or 25
years old, or even today.

00:03:37.074 --> 00:03:39.795
I'm constantly working to reinvent myself.

00:03:39.795 --> 00:03:42.536
I'm not any different
than a package on a shelf.

00:03:42.536 --> 00:03:44.728
People have to feel that it's relevant.

00:03:44.728 --> 00:03:46.162
They have to see the warning labels.

00:03:46.162 --> 00:03:47.477
They have to understand the contents.

00:03:47.477 --> 00:03:48.605
It has to be appealing.

00:03:48.605 --> 00:03:51.438
It has to provide value to people.

00:03:51.438 --> 00:03:53.413
And so when an entrepreneur has a product

00:03:53.413 --> 00:03:54.707
or a process that they've authored,

00:03:54.707 --> 00:03:56.197
and they're not willing to change it,

00:03:56.197 --> 00:03:58.568
then they're going to
end up like Circuit City,

00:03:58.568 --> 00:04:00.484
or Montgomery Ward,

00:04:00.484 --> 00:04:02.724
or Sears, or Fiat.

00:04:02.724 --> 00:04:04.398
Or whatever these brands are

00:04:04.398 --> 00:04:06.018
that don't exist anymore, right?

00:04:06.018 --> 00:04:09.309
Every single company
in this country today,

00:04:09.309 --> 00:04:11.309
if they're not evolving,

00:04:11.309 --> 00:04:12.857
they're dying.

00:04:12.857 --> 00:04:14.236
And I don't know why an entrepreneur

00:04:14.236 --> 00:04:16.687
would think that they would
be exempt from that process.

00:04:16.687 --> 00:04:18.096
I'm not interested in their ego.

00:04:18.096 --> 00:04:19.466
I'm not interested in their pride.

00:04:19.466 --> 00:04:21.281
I'm not interested in their feelings.

00:04:21.281 --> 00:04:23.840
I'm interested in their
business being successful.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.273
And so, I think not only does
their business have to do it,

00:04:27.273 --> 00:04:32.013
but we, as entrepreneurs
have to do it as well.

00:04:32.013 --> 00:04:34.773
(bright techno music)

00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:36.598
- The break through happens

00:04:36.598 --> 00:04:38.189
by conditioning your mind every day,

00:04:38.189 --> 00:04:40.304
by feeding it a role model, or story.

00:04:40.304 --> 00:04:42.395
It's putting yourself in a peak state,

00:04:42.395 --> 00:04:44.152
when you follow through, by
getting physically strong.

00:04:44.152 --> 00:04:45.660
Its creating a little ritual,

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.681
of doing a little bit each
day, and then you get momentum.

00:04:48.681 --> 00:04:50.040
But, the most important thing of all,

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.441
is what we start out with.

00:04:51.441 --> 00:04:52.695
Why?

00:04:52.695 --> 00:04:53.528
- Absolutely.

00:04:53.528 --> 00:04:54.818
- Why is it a must for you?

00:04:54.818 --> 00:04:56.574
It doesn't have to be
you're against the wall,

00:04:56.574 --> 00:04:58.535
but it has to be something
you're hungry for.

00:04:58.535 --> 00:05:00.098
Cuz the only difference
in people, is hunger.

00:05:00.098 --> 00:05:01.323
And if you're not hungry,

00:05:01.323 --> 00:05:02.906
get around people that are hungry,

00:05:02.906 --> 00:05:03.996
and somethin' will hit you.

00:05:03.996 --> 00:05:04.904
You'll watch a conversation,

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.236
you get around people
that are doin' better

00:05:06.236 --> 00:05:09.737
and all of a sudden you start
goin', uh my life sucks.

00:05:09.737 --> 00:05:11.346
I remember I went to a guy in LA

00:05:11.346 --> 00:05:13.212
it's one of the most well,

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.052
multi-billionaire guy, I'll never forget.

00:05:15.052 --> 00:05:17.477
And I lived in the Del Mar
Castle, and I was really proud.

00:05:17.477 --> 00:05:18.817
That was like the symbol of me,

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:20.543
having taken myself from being poor

00:05:20.543 --> 00:05:22.627
to providing for my
family, this great place.

00:05:22.627 --> 00:05:24.168
It's built from castles in Europe

00:05:24.168 --> 00:05:26.214
overlooking the ocean, not far from you.

00:05:26.214 --> 00:05:27.970
And I went to this guy's
house, he's a billionaire.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.023
He took me down to his wine cellar,

00:05:29.023 --> 00:05:30.698
and I don't even drink wine.

00:05:30.698 --> 00:05:31.531
Went through this whole thing,

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.266
at the end of the night I was depressed.

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.952
I lived in a Del Mar tenement,
as far as I was concerned.

00:05:34.952 --> 00:05:37.465
I really was, I was like,
I live in a crappy place,

00:05:37.465 --> 00:05:39.356
and all my standards changed.

00:05:39.356 --> 00:05:42.240
All of a sudden I wasn't willin'
to settle for living there.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.959
All of a sudden, my back was
to the wall in a different way,

00:05:44.959 --> 00:05:47.452
because as a man, I knew
I was capable of more.

00:05:47.452 --> 00:05:49.082
So people can change their standard

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.616
by gettin' around where it's better.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:53.265
People can change their
standard by gettin' associated.

00:05:53.265 --> 00:05:55.198
What's true like the
bills they got to solve,

00:05:55.198 --> 00:05:56.579
the problems they got to do it.

00:05:56.579 --> 00:05:58.818
Or they can do it because they're excited

00:05:58.818 --> 00:05:59.694
cuz there's somethin'
new they want to take on.

00:05:59.694 --> 00:06:02.092
Everyone's different, but
they got to find the why

00:06:02.092 --> 00:06:03.075
and they got to come up with some

00:06:03.075 --> 00:06:04.800
daily rituals to get 'em goin'.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.402
And just do a step at a time.

00:06:06.402 --> 00:06:07.399
That's where you get momentum.

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:09.117
- When I traveled across the country,

00:06:09.117 --> 00:06:11.232
and I talked to basketball players, right?

00:06:11.232 --> 00:06:12.707
When I talked to football players,

00:06:12.707 --> 00:06:14.077
when I talked to baseball players, right?

00:06:14.077 --> 00:06:15.718
This is what I tell these guys,

00:06:15.718 --> 00:06:18.015
you are this close to goin' to the league

00:06:18.015 --> 00:06:19.983
and makin' your dreams become a reality.

00:06:19.983 --> 00:06:23.621
Do yourself a favor,
don't sabotage yourself.

00:06:23.621 --> 00:06:25.690
Now dudes you got to
hear me, I'm tellin' you,

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.318
reinvent yourself, but
after you reinvent yourself,

00:06:28.318 --> 00:06:30.836
I'm tellin' you, don't sabotage yourself.

00:06:30.836 --> 00:06:31.669
What do you mean there?

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:33.335
I tell my boys, listen to me,

00:06:33.335 --> 00:06:34.431
if you don't make it to the NBA,

00:06:34.431 --> 00:06:36.496
let it be because you had an injury.

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:38.193
Not because you got kicked off the team

00:06:38.193 --> 00:06:40.001
because academically you weren't

00:06:40.001 --> 00:06:41.292
where you were supposed to be.

00:06:41.292 --> 00:06:42.756
That's sabotaging yourself.

00:06:42.756 --> 00:06:44.770
Right, don't sleep in, right?

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.180
When you supposed to be at prac--

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.673
that's sabotaging yourself.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.245
Don't get a DUI, don't
get kicked off the team

00:06:50.245 --> 00:06:52.161
because you've broken some school policy,

00:06:52.161 --> 00:06:53.990
or some teeny poli--

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:55.849
that's sabotaging yourself.

00:06:55.849 --> 00:06:59.715
If you get kicked off, let it
be because you put in 120%,

00:06:59.715 --> 00:07:01.240
somebody was better than you.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.093
Or somethin' happened to you physically,

00:07:03.093 --> 00:07:04.320
and so you couldn't stay in the game.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.226
But don't sabotage yourself.

00:07:06.226 --> 00:07:07.339
You say, Eric, what d'ya mean?

00:07:07.339 --> 00:07:10.379
Don't sabotage yourself, by
pushin' the snooze button.

00:07:10.379 --> 00:07:11.693
Don't do it man.

00:07:11.693 --> 00:07:12.541
When you tell yourself

00:07:12.541 --> 00:07:14.297
you goin' wake up at five
o'clock in the mornin'.

00:07:14.297 --> 00:07:16.254
You look at the clock
and it's five o clock,

00:07:16.254 --> 00:07:18.012
don't sabotage yourself
by pushin' the snooze.

00:07:18.012 --> 00:07:20.966
Don't sabotage yourself
by comin' to class late.

00:07:20.966 --> 00:07:23.594
Don't sabotage, get there on time.

00:07:23.594 --> 00:07:26.131
As a matter of fact, the
Vince Lombardi rule says

00:07:26.131 --> 00:07:28.702
if you get there 10
minutes early, you on time.

00:07:28.702 --> 00:07:31.124
If you get there on
time, you already late.

00:07:31.124 --> 00:07:32.642
Don't sabotage your success.

00:07:32.642 --> 00:07:35.116
When you get in there, put all your heart,

00:07:35.116 --> 00:07:37.125
put all your mind, put all your soul.

00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:39.317
And at the end of the day you put in 120

00:07:39.317 --> 00:07:40.625
and you still didn't get a A,

00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:42.980
you got a B, or you got a C.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.504
At least you can walk away feeling good

00:07:44.504 --> 00:07:47.727
knowin' that you put everything
you got on the table.

00:07:47.727 --> 00:07:49.842
You put forth 120%.

00:07:49.842 --> 00:07:51.625
So don't sabotage yourself

00:07:51.625 --> 00:07:53.421
by hangin' out with the wrong people.

00:07:53.421 --> 00:07:56.057
Remember, birds of a
feather flock together

00:07:56.057 --> 00:07:59.540
and eagles and pigeons don't
hang out together, baby.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.600
Alright, once again, it's your boy ET.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:04.724
And remember, baby,
today is your day, man.

00:08:04.724 --> 00:08:08.033
Today is the beginning
of a brand new life.

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:09.565
Today is the beginning of makin'

00:08:09.565 --> 00:08:12.132
all your dreams become a reality.

00:08:12.132 --> 00:08:13.058
And how do I know?

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:13.933
How do I know?

00:08:13.933 --> 00:08:15.485
Cuz I started off as a
high school drop out.

00:08:15.485 --> 00:08:17.891
I started as somebody who was homeless.

00:08:17.891 --> 00:08:20.817
I started from the
bottom, and by God's grace

00:08:20.817 --> 00:08:22.916
worked my way up to the top, baby.

00:08:22.916 --> 00:08:25.183
So, if I can do it, you can do it.

00:08:25.183 --> 00:08:27.073
But listen to me, you got to understand

00:08:27.073 --> 00:08:29.429
that the only way through
storm, count on joy.

00:08:29.429 --> 00:08:31.419
If you in the storm, count it joy.

00:08:31.419 --> 00:08:34.300
If you comin' out of
the storm, count it joy.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.225
Cuz it ain't about the
storm it's about your heart.

00:08:37.225 --> 00:08:40.224
It's about your mind,
it's about your effort.

00:08:40.224 --> 00:08:41.796
Everybody goes through storms.

00:08:41.796 --> 00:08:42.780
Are you listenin' to me?

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:45.588
As ET was blowin' up, my mother-in-law

00:08:45.588 --> 00:08:47.779
got diagnosed with terminal cancer,

00:08:47.779 --> 00:08:49.612
and they told her she was supposed

00:08:49.612 --> 00:08:51.665
to die last December
and she's still livin'.

00:08:51.665 --> 00:08:53.420
My number one fan Susan Turner,

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.899
while I was blowin' up
on YouTube, she was dyin.

00:08:55.899 --> 00:08:58.165
Are you hearin' what I'm sayin' to you?

00:08:58.165 --> 00:09:01.599
Life happens, but when
the tough get goin',

00:09:01.599 --> 00:09:03.659
when things get tough, man.

00:09:03.659 --> 00:09:06.240
When things get tough,
the tough get goin'.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.473
And I like my man Tim, Tim put it best.

00:09:08.473 --> 00:09:11.661
Tim said, "When you goin'
through trials and tribulations,

00:09:11.661 --> 00:09:13.836
"the best thing you can do is handle it.

00:09:13.836 --> 00:09:15.596
"The worst thing you can do is panic.

00:09:15.596 --> 00:09:18.035
"Use it to your advantage."

00:09:18.035 --> 00:09:20.609
Why? Because if you've ever
studied that eagle, baby,

00:09:20.609 --> 00:09:22.933
what you know about that eagle is

00:09:22.933 --> 00:09:25.963
the eagle flies best when there's
storms when there's winds.

00:09:25.963 --> 00:09:27.325
Because what does the eagle do?

00:09:27.325 --> 00:09:28.910
It doesn't have to flap.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.051
What it does is it uses the wind

00:09:31.051 --> 00:09:33.501
from the storm to push it and elevate it.

00:09:33.501 --> 00:09:35.220
And so, I'm here to tell you today, baby,

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.620
I don't care what your trials are,

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.075
what your tribulations are.

00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:40.783
Elevates like that airplane.

00:09:40.783 --> 00:09:42.750
Get beyond the clouds,

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:43.825
elevates.

00:09:43.825 --> 00:09:45.356
Don't worry about your haters.

00:09:45.356 --> 00:09:47.655
Your haters are like
pigeons and guess what?

00:09:47.655 --> 00:09:49.255
Pigeons can only fly so high.

00:09:49.255 --> 00:09:50.741
So you don't have to worry about people,

00:09:50.741 --> 00:09:52.406
and circumstances, and situations.

00:09:52.406 --> 00:09:56.272
You just fly to a place
that they can't go to.

00:09:56.272 --> 00:09:58.330
You elevate yourself when you fly

00:09:58.330 --> 00:09:59.991
to a place that nobody else can go to

00:09:59.991 --> 00:10:02.171
but those who are
willing to be successful.

00:10:02.171 --> 00:10:04.704
- My career, my entire career,

00:10:04.704 --> 00:10:06.732
is a study in reinvention.

00:10:06.732 --> 00:10:09.541
Ya know I started out as
a comedian, that was it.

00:10:09.541 --> 00:10:13.241
I never planned on hosting a radio show,

00:10:13.241 --> 00:10:15.299
hostin' a game show,

00:10:15.299 --> 00:10:17.223
or hostin' a day time talk show.

00:10:17.223 --> 00:10:18.056
I never did.

00:10:18.056 --> 00:10:20.275
Writing books? None of it.

00:10:20.275 --> 00:10:22.302
Making movies. None of it.

00:10:22.302 --> 00:10:26.459
Reinvention happens, when
you diversify your gift.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:29.142
There lies your greatest
secret for success.

00:10:29.142 --> 00:10:32.634
You've got to discover your
gift and when you discover it

00:10:32.634 --> 00:10:35.897
you got to soak it, you
got to wring it out, man.

00:10:35.897 --> 00:10:37.769
You got to diversify it.

00:10:37.769 --> 00:10:40.525
Most of us only have one talent.

00:10:40.525 --> 00:10:42.921
But do you know that that's all you need?

00:10:42.921 --> 00:10:45.965
Mine happens to be to take information

00:10:45.965 --> 00:10:50.178
and immediately transfer it
into other kinds of platforms.

00:10:50.178 --> 00:10:53.244
Now when I was younger, I actually thought

00:10:53.244 --> 00:10:55.259
that I could only do that with comedy.

00:10:55.259 --> 00:10:57.034
But as I've gotten older,

00:10:57.034 --> 00:10:59.384
I discovered through diversification

00:10:59.384 --> 00:11:01.366
that it was a little bit more than that.

00:11:01.366 --> 00:11:03.978
That I could also take
information, immediately,

00:11:03.978 --> 00:11:06.232
transfer it into inspiration.

00:11:06.232 --> 00:11:07.907
I could turn it into motivation,

00:11:07.907 --> 00:11:10.122
I can offer it as guidance.

00:11:10.122 --> 00:11:12.438
So now sittin' on a talk show,

00:11:12.438 --> 00:11:14.114
I actually have somethin' to talk about.

00:11:14.114 --> 00:11:15.434
All the failed marriages.

00:11:15.434 --> 00:11:17.208
I got somethin' to talk about.

00:11:17.208 --> 00:11:19.370
The bein' homeless, I got
somethin' to talk about.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:21.991
Bein' dead broke, I got
somethin' to talk about.

00:11:21.991 --> 00:11:24.282
Havin' bad credit, tax problems,

00:11:24.282 --> 00:11:25.646
I got somethin' to talk about.

00:11:25.646 --> 00:11:26.704
Whatever hole you been in

00:11:26.704 --> 00:11:28.542
I can just about drug myself through it.

00:11:28.542 --> 00:11:30.992
But I came out of all of it because

00:11:30.992 --> 00:11:32.992
I was not afraid

00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:35.359
to diversify my gift.

00:11:35.359 --> 00:11:37.719
Even the book, Act Like
a Lady Think Like a Man,

00:11:37.719 --> 00:11:39.820
it was all about me diversifying a gift.

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:42.764
Okay, I had taken two failed marriages,

00:11:42.764 --> 00:11:46.963
and I had taken the love for my daughters,

00:11:46.963 --> 00:11:48.771
and I combined those things.

00:11:48.771 --> 00:11:52.504
I taught my daughters,
what I knew about men.

00:11:52.504 --> 00:11:55.485
Now little did I discover,
that I had a little over

00:11:55.485 --> 00:11:58.700
four million daughters in this country.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.672
Cousins and nieces and stuff like that

00:12:00.672 --> 00:12:02.368
who needed that same information.

00:12:02.368 --> 00:12:04.256
And that was a huge part for me,

00:12:04.256 --> 00:12:06.769
to take that information
and turn it into a book

00:12:06.769 --> 00:12:10.185
that turned it into a mega star movie.

00:12:10.185 --> 00:12:12.252
And it produced a lot of things for me,

00:12:12.252 --> 00:12:13.939
but it also helped a lot of people.

00:12:13.939 --> 00:12:16.964
One of the other tricks
for reinventing yourself,

00:12:16.964 --> 00:12:20.761
is not letting your background
become a limitation.

00:12:20.761 --> 00:12:24.858
If you take that
background that you're from

00:12:24.858 --> 00:12:29.474
and never let it define you,
but allow it to redefine you

00:12:29.474 --> 00:12:30.994
all that stuff works for the good.

00:12:30.994 --> 00:12:32.819
Do you understand that you needed

00:12:32.819 --> 00:12:34.328
everything that's happened to you,

00:12:34.328 --> 00:12:36.836
to happen to you in the exact
order that it's happened

00:12:36.836 --> 00:12:39.387
in order for you to be the
person that you are today?

00:12:39.387 --> 00:12:42.158
All that failin' and gettin'
over, you needed all of that.

00:12:42.158 --> 00:12:45.001
(audience applauding)

00:12:45.001 --> 00:12:48.922
So it's good to be steeped in
the traditions of your gift

00:12:48.922 --> 00:12:51.027
but don't get stuck in 'em.

00:12:51.027 --> 00:12:52.609
Look if your gift is baking,

00:12:52.609 --> 00:12:56.298
don't assume that there's
only one way to do it.

00:12:56.298 --> 00:12:57.133
If you bake, bake.

00:12:57.133 --> 00:12:59.693
But you can't just bake
for people you know,

00:12:59.693 --> 00:13:01.226
bake for people you don't know.

00:13:01.226 --> 00:13:02.901
You're a musician, let yourself

00:13:02.901 --> 00:13:04.929
explore other types of music.

00:13:04.929 --> 00:13:06.812
I'll tell ya example, The Roots,

00:13:06.812 --> 00:13:08.630
who play on Jimmy Fallon's show.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:13.292
They steeped in hip-hop, but
they're also great musicians.

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:15.042
So what they do is, they take all

00:13:15.042 --> 00:13:18.510
of that talent and now guess what?

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:20.693
Hip-hop, jazz, R&amp;B,

00:13:20.693 --> 00:13:22.276
classic, pop, rock.

00:13:23.616 --> 00:13:24.906
They didn't just get stuck on hip,

00:13:24.906 --> 00:13:26.439
I'm doin' hip-hop, that's it.

00:13:26.439 --> 00:13:27.622
Nah, they do whatever.

00:13:27.622 --> 00:13:28.904
LL Cool J. Hip-hop.

00:13:28.904 --> 00:13:30.895
One of the top actors on TV today.

00:13:30.895 --> 00:13:34.308
Queen Latifa, hip-hop, big
actor right now, ya get it?

00:13:34.308 --> 00:13:37.335
Jerry Seinfeld, nothin' but a comedian,

00:13:37.335 --> 00:13:39.269
one of the biggest actors on TV today.

00:13:39.269 --> 00:13:41.319
Remember, you can win if you're

00:13:41.319 --> 00:13:43.331
not afraid to reinvent yourself.

00:13:43.331 --> 00:13:44.673
Stop gettin' stuck.

00:13:44.673 --> 00:13:46.623
Just go ahead and give
it a try, ya never know.

00:13:46.623 --> 00:13:49.993
- So how do we cultivate this
idea of kind of reinventing

00:13:49.993 --> 00:13:52.519
but its more like, innovative
ideas for ourselves

00:13:52.519 --> 00:13:53.639
to create something new.

00:13:53.639 --> 00:13:56.329
How do we cultivate
these innovative ideas?

00:13:56.329 --> 00:13:58.099
- Well let me ask you a question.

00:13:58.099 --> 00:14:00.151
When you switched into, I don't know,

00:14:00.151 --> 00:14:02.142
did you play handball
since you were a kid?

00:14:02.142 --> 00:14:02.975
- [Lewis] No.

00:14:02.975 --> 00:14:04.325
- Okay so how did you decide

00:14:04.325 --> 00:14:07.720
I'm going to be an Olympic
level athlete in handball?

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:09.162
- Sure.
- and...

00:14:09.162 --> 00:14:11.274
what was the first thing you did?

00:14:11.274 --> 00:14:13.562
- I saw it on TV, I
watched the 2008 Olympics.

00:14:13.562 --> 00:14:15.330
I was sleeping on my sister's couch still.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.180
With the, I'd just gotten my cast off

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.743
from playing football, from a surgery.

00:14:18.743 --> 00:14:20.984
And I watched some Olympics and it,

00:14:20.984 --> 00:14:23.152
instantly I just had a new idea.

00:14:23.152 --> 00:14:24.662
I said that's something I want to do.

00:14:24.662 --> 00:14:26.535
I just like, I want to play on the USA.

00:14:26.535 --> 00:14:27.368
- So, so something..

00:14:27.368 --> 00:14:28.201
stirred inside you?

00:14:28.201 --> 00:14:29.283
- [Lewis] Yes, yes.

00:14:29.283 --> 00:14:30.116
- Like, you felt it.

00:14:30.116 --> 00:14:31.785
- [Lewis] It was like a dream,
a new dream was created.

00:14:31.785 --> 00:14:34.800
- And that happens to people,
I don't want to say every day,

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.050
but like, once a year,
a couple times a year,

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.196
once a month that you feel that

00:14:38.196 --> 00:14:39.428
and you don't always
pursue everything, right?

00:14:39.428 --> 00:14:40.261
- [Lewis] Right.

00:14:40.261 --> 00:14:41.508
- I'm sure there's many
things you would like

00:14:41.508 --> 00:14:42.341
to do that you don't pursue.

00:14:42.341 --> 00:14:43.476
- Don't have the bandwidth for,

00:14:43.476 --> 00:14:44.995
or it's not the right
timing or whatever, yeah.

00:14:44.995 --> 00:14:46.603
- [James] But you already
had training as an athlete.

00:14:46.603 --> 00:14:47.436
- Yes.

00:14:47.436 --> 00:14:48.971
- So you knew okay this is another sport.

00:14:48.971 --> 00:14:50.396
This is something where I hit, it's almost

00:14:50.396 --> 00:14:52.152
like a back door to the Olympics because,

00:14:52.152 --> 00:14:52.985
- [Lewis] Yes.

00:14:52.985 --> 00:14:53.818
- or to the US team,

00:14:53.818 --> 00:14:56.154
because who else would think to do this.

00:14:56.154 --> 00:14:57.374
- [Lewis] No one else is playing, yeah...

00:14:57.374 --> 00:14:58.845
- So, it seems like an old man

00:14:58.845 --> 00:15:01.186
swearing I can probably squeeze
in here and get good enough.

00:15:01.186 --> 00:15:03.326
Okay, so what'd you do next?

00:15:03.326 --> 00:15:04.972
- So next, I started researching.

00:15:04.972 --> 00:15:07.591
I went online and started
researching like USA handball,

00:15:07.591 --> 00:15:10.080
handball teams in Ohio,
there was nothing in Ohio.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:12.623
Then I said okay where are
the teams in the country?

00:15:12.623 --> 00:15:15.975
And then I started looking at
like what are the best teams?

00:15:15.975 --> 00:15:17.685
cuz if I'm going to learn this quickly,

00:15:17.685 --> 00:15:18.518
I need to learn from the best.

00:15:18.518 --> 00:15:20.367
So I learned that the New York team,

00:15:20.367 --> 00:15:23.909
had won the national championships
over the last few years.

00:15:23.909 --> 00:15:26.067
So I was like okay when
I make enough money,

00:15:26.067 --> 00:15:27.925
I'm going to go to New
York City and learn from

00:15:27.925 --> 00:15:29.166
these players, this team.

00:15:29.166 --> 00:15:31.557
And for about the next year,

00:15:31.557 --> 00:15:32.855
I was like well how am I going to do that?

00:15:32.855 --> 00:15:35.151
Cuz I have no money, I'm
broke on my sister's couch.

00:15:35.151 --> 00:15:37.957
That's when LinkedIn started
kind of opening up for me.

00:15:37.957 --> 00:15:39.748
And I started to make,
like a few hundred bucks

00:15:39.748 --> 00:15:41.235
a month teaching LinkedIn.

00:15:41.235 --> 00:15:43.991
So I said, okay, when I make
enough money doing this,

00:15:43.991 --> 00:15:46.574
then I'm going to leave Ohio
and go to New York City.

00:15:46.574 --> 00:15:48.348
To like, see what this is like.

00:15:48.348 --> 00:15:49.181
- And by the way, when
you were in New York City,

00:15:49.181 --> 00:15:51.441
it's not like you stopped
making money on LinkedIn.

00:15:51.441 --> 00:15:52.642
- [Lewis] No, no, I was still doing that.

00:15:52.642 --> 00:15:53.475
- These things are
interweaving each other.

00:15:53.475 --> 00:15:54.308
- They're all interweaving, yes.

00:15:54.308 --> 00:15:57.838
So I about a year later,
a year and a half later,

00:15:57.838 --> 00:16:00.514
I started really making a lot of money

00:16:00.514 --> 00:16:02.372
like just kind of started happening.

00:16:02.372 --> 00:16:04.072
Everything started to unfold and happen

00:16:04.072 --> 00:16:05.547
after a lot of action taking.

00:16:05.547 --> 00:16:07.518
And so I moved to New
York City for a month.

00:16:07.518 --> 00:16:10.105
Now at the whole time for
this year, year and a half,

00:16:10.105 --> 00:16:11.546
no one would respond to me on

00:16:11.546 --> 00:16:13.434
the USA national team for
like the headquarters.

00:16:13.434 --> 00:16:16.175
No one would respond to
me at the New York team.

00:16:16.175 --> 00:16:18.028
I would email people,
I would call numbers,

00:16:18.028 --> 00:16:19.479
no one would get back to me.

00:16:19.479 --> 00:16:21.136
- How were you getting
better during this time?

00:16:21.136 --> 00:16:22.346
- I was just training as an athlete,

00:16:22.346 --> 00:16:24.452
but I still hadn't played handball yet.

00:16:24.452 --> 00:16:26.277
But I still had this idea of like,

00:16:26.277 --> 00:16:28.075
I need to go and at least explore it,

00:16:28.075 --> 00:16:31.448
so I don't regret not trying
to see if I could make this.

00:16:31.448 --> 00:16:32.995
I was like at least I got to go and try it

00:16:32.995 --> 00:16:34.878
so I can kind of eliminate it from my mind

00:16:34.878 --> 00:16:38.398
as something I want to do or I
don't want to do in the future.

00:16:38.398 --> 00:16:40.031
But for me personally, I know that if

00:16:40.031 --> 00:16:41.823
I think about something, I want to do it

00:16:41.823 --> 00:16:43.847
and if I don't at least explore it

00:16:43.847 --> 00:16:45.400
I'll think about it
for the rest of my life

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.761
and I'll regret not trying.

00:16:46.761 --> 00:16:47.683
Not giving it a go.
- Right

00:16:47.683 --> 00:16:51.333
- So I said okay, no one's
getting back to me anywhere.

00:16:51.333 --> 00:16:52.573
I'm emailing people every month.

00:16:52.573 --> 00:16:53.989
I'm trying to call people every month,

00:16:53.989 --> 00:16:55.552
no one's getting back to me.

00:16:55.552 --> 00:16:58.395
So I say screw it, I'm going
to go to New York for a month.

00:16:58.395 --> 00:16:59.921
I had a couple of
speaking gigs in New York

00:16:59.921 --> 00:17:01.843
for like LinkedIn something,

00:17:01.843 --> 00:17:03.385
and had some social media conferences.

00:17:03.385 --> 00:17:05.109
And I was like, I'm just
going to go stay for the month

00:17:05.109 --> 00:17:06.653
and I'm going to show
up at their practice.

00:17:06.653 --> 00:17:08.445
Cuz they had the practice address

00:17:08.445 --> 00:17:12.324
of where they practice on the
website for the New York team.

00:17:12.324 --> 00:17:14.196
- So you got ready.

00:17:14.196 --> 00:17:15.525
- [Lewis] I got ready.

00:17:15.525 --> 00:17:17.655
- By constantly training.
- Training, yep.

00:17:17.655 --> 00:17:19.373
- And then you just you fired.

00:17:19.373 --> 00:17:20.930
- That's it, I just showed up.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:21.987
And I showed up at practice

00:17:21.987 --> 00:17:22.820
when they said they were playing,

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:23.681
cuz no one picked up or got back to me.

00:17:23.681 --> 00:17:25.472
- [James] No one gave you
permission to do that.

00:17:25.472 --> 00:17:26.447
- No one gave me permission.

00:17:26.447 --> 00:17:27.547
I showed up and the first day I got there,

00:17:27.547 --> 00:17:31.126
I was the only American
on, who was in the court.

00:17:31.126 --> 00:17:34.267
And it was all these
former professional players

00:17:34.267 --> 00:17:37.333
in Europe, who now moved to
New York and kind of like,

00:17:37.333 --> 00:17:39.102
live and play for fun.

00:17:39.102 --> 00:17:40.427
- So as a white man.
- Yes.

00:17:40.427 --> 00:17:41.540
- You were basically the minority

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.800
on the American team.
- I was the minority.

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:44.599
I was like-- they barely spoke English.

00:17:44.599 --> 00:17:46.549
I was just like this outsider.

00:17:46.549 --> 00:17:48.880
And I got there and I go,

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:49.968
hey guys, my name's Lewis,

00:17:49.968 --> 00:17:50.943
I'm here from Ohio

00:17:50.943 --> 00:17:52.670
and my goal is to make the Olympics

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:53.991
and play with the USA national team.

00:17:53.991 --> 00:17:55.608
And they just all started laughing.

00:17:55.608 --> 00:17:57.526
And then I just showed
up every single week.

00:17:57.526 --> 00:17:59.160
I ended up moving there, to New York.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.960
I didn't go back to
Ohio, I stayed there for

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.462
the next year and a half.

00:18:02.462 --> 00:18:04.131
And nine months later I made the USA team.

00:18:04.131 --> 00:18:06.095
But I was there every
single week practicing

00:18:06.095 --> 00:18:08.867
and just like learning
and taking action and--

00:18:08.867 --> 00:18:10.271
- So what you did was,

00:18:10.271 --> 00:18:12.912
exemplifies something that I,

00:18:12.912 --> 00:18:14.082
and this isn't original to me

00:18:14.082 --> 00:18:15.951
I'll describe where it comes from

00:18:15.951 --> 00:18:19.719
but I call, in my book, I call this,

00:18:19.719 --> 00:18:23.391
you reinvent yourself by
finding your plus-minus-equal.

00:18:23.391 --> 00:18:26.731
So your plus was all these people,

00:18:26.731 --> 00:18:29.361
you wanted to be around
the best in the world

00:18:29.361 --> 00:18:30.469
- [Lewis] People better than me.

00:18:30.469 --> 00:18:31.537
- Right so you could learn from them.

00:18:31.537 --> 00:18:32.614
So you have to find your plus.

00:18:32.614 --> 00:18:34.381
And at first they're virtual.

00:18:34.381 --> 00:18:36.344
You maybe watch YouTube videos about them,

00:18:36.344 --> 00:18:37.556
you read books about them.

00:18:37.556 --> 00:18:40.985
You study things that they
write, or photographs they take

00:18:40.985 --> 00:18:42.651
or videos they shoot.

00:18:42.651 --> 00:18:44.892
So then they became real for you because

00:18:44.892 --> 00:18:47.503
you actually joined them and
started hanging around them.

00:18:47.503 --> 00:18:49.340
Then you have to find your equals.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:51.381
Because if you're just crushed every day

00:18:51.381 --> 00:18:53.323
in a game of handball, it's
going to be hard for you.

00:18:53.323 --> 00:18:54.214
You need lessons, but then you need

00:18:54.214 --> 00:18:55.364
people who challenge you.

00:18:55.364 --> 00:18:56.197
- [Lewis] Yes.

00:18:56.197 --> 00:18:58.030
- So people who you can say ugh, I got

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:59.482
that one more point off
him, I feel challenged.

00:18:59.482 --> 00:19:01.138
Then you get better and better,

00:19:01.138 --> 00:19:02.359
and you can measure your results.

00:19:02.359 --> 00:19:03.192
- And there were people
there that were like that,

00:19:03.192 --> 00:19:05.398
who on the team were kind
of beginners so I was--

00:19:05.398 --> 00:19:07.316
- Right. So you found your peer group.

00:19:07.316 --> 00:19:08.166
- Right
- You found...

00:19:08.166 --> 00:19:09.403
your new cohort.

00:19:09.403 --> 00:19:12.301
And then you find kind of,
its almost a bad word for it,

00:19:12.301 --> 00:19:14.189
but you call it, I call it the minus.

00:19:14.189 --> 00:19:15.787
Which is people you could teach.

00:19:15.787 --> 00:19:17.662
I don't know if this was like,

00:19:17.662 --> 00:19:19.857
a catalyst for your reinvention.

00:19:19.857 --> 00:19:21.790
But ultimately, you
play people in handball,

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:22.878
that you're a lot better than.

00:19:22.878 --> 00:19:25.417
Then you could teach them and
that solidifies your learning.

00:19:25.417 --> 00:19:26.250
- [Lewis] Right.

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:27.612
- So and that's almost every reinvention,

00:19:27.612 --> 00:19:29.186
ya know you and I have both had

00:19:29.186 --> 00:19:30.529
hundreds of people on our podcasts

00:19:30.529 --> 00:19:31.980
they've all reinvented themselves.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.646
And I bet you in every single case,

00:19:33.646 --> 00:19:35.150
there's a plus-minus-equal.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.015
- [Lewis] Yeah, I'm sure.

00:19:36.015 --> 00:19:38.373
- So that happens with all of
'em, like I talk to anybody

00:19:38.373 --> 00:19:41.834
from a rapper, to a huge entrepreneur,

00:19:41.834 --> 00:19:42.882
like a billionaire entrepreneur.

00:19:42.882 --> 00:19:44.740
They've all had their plus-minus-equal.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.731
- What are some of the steps

00:19:46.731 --> 00:19:48.754
that you guide people through

00:19:48.754 --> 00:19:52.362
of how they can reinvent themselves?

00:19:52.362 --> 00:19:55.227
- Well again, everybody wants
the sort of quick, magic pill

00:19:55.227 --> 00:19:57.372
and I think in the time that
we've got available here,

00:19:57.372 --> 00:19:58.998
what I really want to do is guide people

00:19:58.998 --> 00:20:02.764
into some areas of focus that
can really add some value.

00:20:02.764 --> 00:20:04.933
And the first one that I always pick,

00:20:04.933 --> 00:20:07.615
is about asking better questions.

00:20:07.615 --> 00:20:09.782
Yeah, questions direct our focus.

00:20:10.895 --> 00:20:13.598
And if you're not direct
in your own focus,

00:20:13.598 --> 00:20:15.338
I've got news for you,
there's a lot of people

00:20:15.338 --> 00:20:17.889
that pay a lot of good
money to Madison Avenue

00:20:17.889 --> 00:20:19.758
to ya know figure out
how to do it for you.

00:20:19.758 --> 00:20:21.291
- Right.

00:20:21.291 --> 00:20:23.070
- And, that's not the life we want to live

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.809
being programmed by
other people's agendas.

00:20:25.809 --> 00:20:29.186
And I liken the mind to a compass needle.

00:20:29.186 --> 00:20:32.833
It can only point in
one direction at a time.

00:20:32.833 --> 00:20:34.824
And the challenge is just like if

00:20:34.824 --> 00:20:38.767
we take a needle and magnetize
it, like back in high school.

00:20:38.767 --> 00:20:42.677
You take a magnet, a power
source and you align it

00:20:42.677 --> 00:20:45.544
and keep stroking that needle
in one continuous direction

00:20:45.544 --> 00:20:48.153
so that needle aligns
to the magnetic field.

00:20:48.153 --> 00:20:50.136
And becomes coherent pointed

00:20:50.136 --> 00:20:52.269
now all of the ions
point in one direction,

00:20:52.269 --> 00:20:54.109
it becomes magnetized.

00:20:54.109 --> 00:20:55.959
Now our mind is very similar.

00:20:55.959 --> 00:21:00.421
Now if we are open to
unconsciously being programmed,

00:21:00.421 --> 00:21:01.487
which unfortunately as human beings,

00:21:01.487 --> 00:21:03.820
we are you know we're a 24/7

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:06.283
constant adaptation machine.

00:21:06.283 --> 00:21:08.985
Now our mind and our body,

00:21:08.985 --> 00:21:11.503
Now we understand the
body part that's easy

00:21:11.503 --> 00:21:12.864
now the physical side
of life everybody gets

00:21:12.864 --> 00:21:15.544
because they have
experiential, now evidence of.

00:21:15.544 --> 00:21:18.352
Now your body will adapt if
you put it in McDonald's,

00:21:18.352 --> 00:21:19.557
or if you put it in the gym.

00:21:19.557 --> 00:21:22.822
It doesn't mind, it will adapt
accordingly, that's its job.

00:21:22.822 --> 00:21:25.089
But our mind is far more programmable,

00:21:25.089 --> 00:21:27.802
far quicker than our body.

00:21:27.802 --> 00:21:29.294
And if the magnet

00:21:29.294 --> 00:21:30.878
that the strong force

00:21:30.878 --> 00:21:33.069
that's constantly magnetizing us,

00:21:33.069 --> 00:21:36.061
is usually the media and our peer group.

00:21:36.061 --> 00:21:38.846
And if those two aren't optimal

00:21:38.846 --> 00:21:43.101
then ya know were going to
be sucked along for the ride

00:21:43.101 --> 00:21:47.693
and don't really magnetize
our true north for ourselves.

00:21:47.693 --> 00:21:50.171
So by asking better questions,

00:21:50.171 --> 00:21:53.178
what it does it shifts the
direction of that needle.

00:21:53.178 --> 00:21:56.101
Now the challenge is, you
can only do that for 10%

00:21:56.101 --> 00:21:57.351
of the time that you're conscious,

00:21:57.351 --> 00:22:01.216
or sleeping awake is how most
people are 90% of the time.

00:22:01.216 --> 00:22:02.904
You ask why when we're driving to work

00:22:02.904 --> 00:22:05.267
we can't remember the last
two kilometers on the freeway,

00:22:05.267 --> 00:22:07.376
you know, what happened? (laughs)

00:22:07.376 --> 00:22:10.099
But, now if we focus on
being able to magnetize

00:22:10.099 --> 00:22:11.521
or take charge of which direction

00:22:11.521 --> 00:22:13.322
our compass needle is pointing,

00:22:13.322 --> 00:22:15.690
we have a chance to start
reinventing ourselves.

00:22:15.690 --> 00:22:19.367
Because otherwise yeah again,
you're going to be drifting,

00:22:19.367 --> 00:22:21.266
especially in that 90% of the time when we

00:22:21.266 --> 00:22:23.649
do things out of habit, unconsciously.

00:22:23.649 --> 00:22:25.757
That compass needle drifts back

00:22:25.757 --> 00:22:27.686
to it's preconditioned magnetic north.

00:22:27.686 --> 00:22:29.981
And most the time that doesn't serve us.

00:22:29.981 --> 00:22:31.797
Whether it's media conditioned,

00:22:31.797 --> 00:22:33.946
paper conditioned, and you
know society conditioned.

00:22:33.946 --> 00:22:35.345
You know, look out of your window,

00:22:35.345 --> 00:22:36.828
there's not many examples of

00:22:36.828 --> 00:22:38.221
who we want to emulate and become

00:22:38.221 --> 00:22:40.405
that surround us on a day-to-day basis.

00:22:40.405 --> 00:22:42.446
So ya know the first question is,

00:22:42.446 --> 00:22:45.014
or the first step is ask better questions.

00:22:45.014 --> 00:22:47.155
Yeah, and what ignites you?

00:22:47.155 --> 00:22:50.832
What causes you to come from a place of

00:22:50.832 --> 00:22:52.701
wanting to really give your gift,

00:22:52.701 --> 00:22:54.862
not survive in today's world,

00:22:54.862 --> 00:22:56.500
cuz you got a mortgage to make.

00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:57.946
Not take the path of certainty

00:22:57.946 --> 00:22:59.226
which if the entrepreneurs,

00:22:59.226 --> 00:23:00.547
if they haven't figured it out yet is,

00:23:00.547 --> 00:23:02.834
I'm sure you'll let them know as well,

00:23:02.834 --> 00:23:05.739
that there is no certainty in life.

00:23:05.739 --> 00:23:08.470
Now so the ability to handle uncertainty

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:12.441
is one of the core characteristics
of an entrepreneur.

00:23:12.441 --> 00:23:16.409
And so to be able to do that
ask yourself better questions.

00:23:16.409 --> 00:23:21.066
Now what resources do I
have that I'm not using yet?

00:23:21.066 --> 00:23:23.041
Great question cuz it'll start

00:23:23.041 --> 00:23:24.450
you looking in different areas.

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:26.766
This is one of the best
things about the human brain

00:23:26.766 --> 00:23:29.071
is if you ask a question
it'll give you the answer.

00:23:29.071 --> 00:23:31.575
The challenge is that most
of us ask lousy questions.

00:23:31.575 --> 00:23:33.484
Yeah, why's this always happen to me?

00:23:33.484 --> 00:23:34.712
And it'll give you an answer.

00:23:34.712 --> 00:23:35.931
It's programmed to, right?

00:23:35.931 --> 00:23:37.806
Because you're worthless,
because you deserve it,

00:23:37.806 --> 00:23:40.157
because you're not smart enough and all...

00:23:40.157 --> 00:23:41.757
So by asking better questions,

00:23:41.757 --> 00:23:42.950
we can search for better answers,

00:23:42.950 --> 00:23:45.424
and that's really the
first place to start.

00:23:45.424 --> 00:23:46.341
- I love it.

00:23:46.341 --> 00:23:48.013
Is there a series of questions

00:23:48.013 --> 00:23:50.718
that you recommend
everybody ask themselves?

00:23:50.718 --> 00:23:52.490
Kind of regardless of their situation?

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:55.306
So that what ignites me,
what gives me passion,

00:23:55.306 --> 00:23:58.862
what resources do I have
that I'm not currently using

00:23:58.862 --> 00:24:00.671
are some that you mentioned.

00:24:00.671 --> 00:24:01.925
Are there others that you recommend people

00:24:01.925 --> 00:24:06.103
kind of get into the habit
of asking themselves?

00:24:06.103 --> 00:24:08.246
- Yes, and it really ties
into what our call really

00:24:08.246 --> 00:24:10.973
the next part of gettng into
reinventing who you are.

00:24:10.973 --> 00:24:13.904
And that is to check your why.

00:24:13.904 --> 00:24:16.660
Ya know we're driven by
reasons as human beings.

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:18.181
Yeah everybody does things for reasons.

00:24:18.181 --> 00:24:20.320
Now they may not be your
reasons, may not be my reasons,

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:22.656
but yet we do things for reasons.

00:24:22.656 --> 00:24:24.848
Most of the time unfortunately,

00:24:24.848 --> 00:24:26.919
we do very little out of logical reasons.

00:24:26.919 --> 00:24:29.686
Now we do a fair amount out of passion,

00:24:29.686 --> 00:24:32.348
but most of what we do we do out of habit.

00:24:32.348 --> 00:24:36.194
And those habits are formed
based upon the repetitive

00:24:36.194 --> 00:24:37.829
questions we tend to ask ourself

00:24:37.829 --> 00:24:40.623
which usually are sub-optimum.

00:24:40.623 --> 00:24:42.441
So if you were to ask questions that

00:24:42.441 --> 00:24:44.777
elicited your reason why.

00:24:44.777 --> 00:24:47.630
And here's what I found
in the three decades

00:24:47.630 --> 00:24:49.205
of being an entrepreneur now.

00:24:49.205 --> 00:24:52.374
That is almost universally consistent,

00:24:52.374 --> 00:24:56.351
if your why is focused
on you are not powerful,

00:24:56.351 --> 00:24:58.801
you're not present, you
don't have the ability

00:24:58.801 --> 00:25:01.156
to dig deeper than you could.

00:25:01.156 --> 00:25:03.419
Unless it was rather than if your why

00:25:03.419 --> 00:25:06.803
is focused on something greater than you.

00:25:06.803 --> 00:25:08.844
And yeah we can see this
in evidence everywhere.

00:25:08.844 --> 00:25:10.004
I'll give a classic example.

00:25:10.004 --> 00:25:11.654
You take the New York
or the Boston marathon,

00:25:11.654 --> 00:25:13.991
Boston gets more pros, but
the New York marathon's a goal

00:25:13.991 --> 00:25:18.574
for a lot of people in their
fitness sort of resolutions.

00:25:18.574 --> 00:25:20.039
And for those that haven't ran

00:25:20.039 --> 00:25:21.678
a marathon before its a big goal.

00:25:21.678 --> 00:25:23.517
It takes a lot of
training ya know I've ran

00:25:23.517 --> 00:25:24.980
crazy stuff before and its not easy

00:25:24.980 --> 00:25:26.962
if you're not a professional athlete.

00:25:26.962 --> 00:25:30.587
So if you take New York, 35,000
people lining the streets

00:25:30.587 --> 00:25:33.484
cheering you on, the
amount of people that run

00:25:33.484 --> 00:25:35.446
the New York marathon for the first time

00:25:35.446 --> 00:25:37.684
not the people who do it for fun,

00:25:37.684 --> 00:25:40.544
or as an athlete on a regular
basis, but for the first time.

00:25:40.544 --> 00:25:43.509
There is way more percentage
of those people that complete

00:25:43.509 --> 00:25:47.710
the marathon that are
running for something else.

00:25:47.710 --> 00:25:49.558
Not themselves, not
their ego, not the medal,

00:25:49.558 --> 00:25:52.081
not significance, not the bragging rights.

00:25:52.081 --> 00:25:54.289
To support somebody they loved,

00:25:54.289 --> 00:25:56.106
in memory of somebody they cared about,

00:25:56.106 --> 00:25:58.652
to raise money for a
cause they believe in,

00:25:58.652 --> 00:26:00.333
something beyond themselves.

00:26:00.333 --> 00:26:02.096
And that's because those that
are running for themselves

00:26:02.096 --> 00:26:05.742
most of those quit before
the day of the marathon.

00:26:05.742 --> 00:26:07.937
It takes a lot to dig deep when you're

00:26:07.937 --> 00:26:10.412
just looking at going out of ego.

00:26:10.412 --> 00:26:14.495
So questions that ask you
to reevaluate your why.

00:26:15.972 --> 00:26:19.332
And most people's why, by default,

00:26:19.332 --> 00:26:20.665
is grounded in a

00:26:25.108 --> 00:26:26.674
an area that's really

00:26:26.674 --> 00:26:27.924
is fear driven.

00:26:29.023 --> 00:26:30.589
What if I fail?

00:26:30.589 --> 00:26:32.325
Therefore my why for doing this because

00:26:32.325 --> 00:26:35.245
I think it's going to give me
the best chance of success.

00:26:35.245 --> 00:26:36.315
Not because I'm passionate about it,

00:26:36.315 --> 00:26:37.952
not because it's giving
my gift to the world,

00:26:37.952 --> 00:26:40.482
not because it's something
I've always wanted to do.

00:26:40.482 --> 00:26:42.477
So asking questions like if I knew

00:26:42.477 --> 00:26:46.328
it was impossible to fail,
what would I do then?

00:26:46.328 --> 00:26:48.561
That removed the fear of failure away

00:26:48.561 --> 00:26:50.721
and opened up possibility thinking.

00:26:50.721 --> 00:26:52.465
And what it'll do it'll start
getting you in touch with

00:26:52.465 --> 00:26:54.473
what inspires you, what lights you up,

00:26:54.473 --> 00:26:58.459
what gives you that lift,
not the motivational factor

00:26:58.459 --> 00:27:00.349
which is usually avoiding pain.

00:27:00.349 --> 00:27:03.965
And needs a will power to get you through

00:27:03.965 --> 00:27:06.181
getting up at 5 a.m. when its cold.

00:27:06.181 --> 00:27:08.980
Inspiration you don't need motivation.

00:27:08.980 --> 00:27:10.561
Motivation is a fuel tank in a car,

00:27:10.561 --> 00:27:12.660
it runs out, it needs topping up.

00:27:12.660 --> 00:27:14.920
Inspiration is a deeper well spring.

00:27:14.920 --> 00:27:16.783
Now asking questions, like if I could only

00:27:16.783 --> 00:27:21.552
spend my life doing one
thing, what would it be?

00:27:21.552 --> 00:27:25.824
And start tuning yourself
in to that passion center

00:27:25.824 --> 00:27:30.477
that a lot of the time we build
bars around to imprison it

00:27:30.477 --> 00:27:34.131
through not having to face
the possibility of failure

00:27:34.131 --> 00:27:36.669
and therefore admit to
ourselves we're not enough.

00:27:36.669 --> 00:27:39.164
Which is usually what I see
with so many entrepreneurs

00:27:39.164 --> 00:27:40.869
that are burning themselves out.

00:27:40.869 --> 00:27:43.643
They're running patterns of
chasing things that they think

00:27:43.643 --> 00:27:45.227
will give them the success that

00:27:45.227 --> 00:27:47.717
will validate them in the eyes of others.

00:27:47.717 --> 00:27:50.356
Whether it's their parents,
their business studies teacher,

00:27:50.356 --> 00:27:51.928
their elder brother who they perceive

00:27:51.928 --> 00:27:53.414
they're always trying
to be in the shadow of.

00:27:53.414 --> 00:27:55.521
It doesn't matter, we've
all got our reasons.

00:27:55.521 --> 00:27:57.853
Whereas if your independence of

00:27:57.853 --> 00:28:00.465
what I call swimming in goop

00:28:00.465 --> 00:28:03.685
G-O-O-P the good opinion of other people.

00:28:03.685 --> 00:28:06.990
Most people spend their
life swimming in goop,

00:28:06.990 --> 00:28:09.512
and its a sticky, nasty
smelly mess that will lead you

00:28:09.512 --> 00:28:12.799
to a fast track to mediocrity and nowhere.

00:28:12.799 --> 00:28:15.418
So if you can escape the
good opinion of other people,

00:28:15.418 --> 00:28:17.161
and stand proud in your truth,

00:28:17.161 --> 00:28:20.915
that win, lose or draw
I'm not taking it with me.

00:28:20.915 --> 00:28:23.621
Ya know the only people that
tried that were the Egyptians.

00:28:23.621 --> 00:28:24.479
And what happened?

00:28:24.479 --> 00:28:26.799
3000 years later we
dug it up and stole it.

00:28:26.799 --> 00:28:29.298
Ya know I'm here to make
the time I've got count.

00:28:29.298 --> 00:28:31.246
I'm here to make a difference,
I'm here to give my gift.

00:28:31.246 --> 00:28:34.978
And you can only do that
with the freedom of being

00:28:34.978 --> 00:28:37.919
independent of the fear
of not being enough,

00:28:37.919 --> 00:28:41.175
or the fear of having to
adapt myself consistently

00:28:41.175 --> 00:28:43.407
like a chameleon to fit the
pictures of what I think other

00:28:43.407 --> 00:28:46.336
people should see me as,
rather than say listen

00:28:46.336 --> 00:28:49.709
yeah, I respect where you're
at, were always going to see

00:28:49.709 --> 00:28:50.975
things differently because that's

00:28:50.975 --> 00:28:51.995
who we are as human beings.

00:28:51.995 --> 00:28:54.061
I'm celebrating my truth
and I'm walking this way,

00:28:54.061 --> 00:28:56.324
and no one's talking me out of it.

00:28:56.324 --> 00:28:57.811
I'm providing that nobody is less than

00:28:57.811 --> 00:28:59.574
because you crossed their path.

00:28:59.574 --> 00:29:01.529
You know there's a moral basis to that.

00:29:01.529 --> 00:29:03.274
Then yeah swing the bat with a smile,

00:29:03.274 --> 00:29:06.060
and strike out or hit a
home run but swing the bat.

00:29:06.060 --> 00:29:07.756
- So my quick take on reinventing yourself

00:29:07.756 --> 00:29:09.715
is that it needs to be a constant.

00:29:09.715 --> 00:29:11.928
This isn't just one thing
that every now and then,

00:29:11.928 --> 00:29:13.611
you reinvent yourself.

00:29:13.611 --> 00:29:16.855
You are constantly evolving
and changing as a human being.

00:29:16.855 --> 00:29:18.942
And the things that you
do, what's scheduled

00:29:18.942 --> 00:29:20.945
into your calendar on a day-to-day basis,

00:29:20.945 --> 00:29:24.551
needs to change and evolve
as you change and evolve.

00:29:24.551 --> 00:29:28.800
I am a extremely rigid, scheduled person.

00:29:28.800 --> 00:29:32.560
If you look at my calendar,
it's packed full of stuff

00:29:32.560 --> 00:29:34.601
that I have to do every single week,

00:29:34.601 --> 00:29:35.834
and I love that schedule.

00:29:35.834 --> 00:29:39.217
But at the same time I'm
very hyper-focused and aware

00:29:39.217 --> 00:29:42.408
of where I feel like
things are out of whack.

00:29:42.408 --> 00:29:44.445
If I feel like I need to spend more time

00:29:44.445 --> 00:29:46.860
on my YouTtube channel, I'm
being pulled in that direction.

00:29:46.860 --> 00:29:48.390
Or I need to spend more time with my wife,

00:29:48.390 --> 00:29:49.910
I'm being puled over here.

00:29:49.910 --> 00:29:52.453
Or I need to spend more
time at TorontoDanceSalsa,

00:29:52.453 --> 00:29:53.335
and I'm pulled this way.

00:29:53.335 --> 00:29:55.088
or I need to spend more time as a father,

00:29:55.088 --> 00:29:56.456
and I'm pulled that way.

00:29:56.456 --> 00:30:00.764
I'm constantly analyzing, and
adjusting and then changing.

00:30:00.764 --> 00:30:03.776
Making modifications in the
schedule to support what I'm

00:30:03.776 --> 00:30:06.156
currently feeling, and
I think too many people,

00:30:06.156 --> 00:30:09.897
your schedule is out of
whack with your priorities.

00:30:09.897 --> 00:30:11.485
Maybe when you first set up your schedule,

00:30:11.485 --> 00:30:13.460
maybe when you first set up your business,

00:30:13.460 --> 00:30:14.954
everything was in alignment.

00:30:14.954 --> 00:30:16.541
Here's what I want to
do, here are my goals,

00:30:16.541 --> 00:30:17.601
here's what's important to
me, here's my priorities.

00:30:17.601 --> 00:30:19.603
Okay great, I'm going to create a schedule

00:30:19.603 --> 00:30:22.568
that's going to focus my efforts
on achieving those goals.

00:30:22.568 --> 00:30:26.587
Amazing, as your priorities
change, as life happens to you,

00:30:26.587 --> 00:30:28.889
you need to adjust your
schedule accordingly,

00:30:28.889 --> 00:30:31.433
or you're going to be unhappy,
you're going to be dissatisfied,

00:30:31.433 --> 00:30:34.119
you're going to constantly be
feeling a pull to go over here,

00:30:34.119 --> 00:30:35.558
but you feel stuck here.

00:30:35.558 --> 00:30:36.890
And as long as you feel stuck here,

00:30:36.890 --> 00:30:38.045
you're never going to be happy.

00:30:38.045 --> 00:30:41.239
And too many people are too
afraid to then make that change.

00:30:41.239 --> 00:30:42.638
As an entrepreneur, you have the

00:30:42.638 --> 00:30:43.981
ultimate freedom to be able to create

00:30:43.981 --> 00:30:45.196
the schedule that you want.

00:30:45.196 --> 00:30:46.124
And if you're not an entrepreneur yet,

00:30:46.124 --> 00:30:48.206
stop blaming other people.

00:30:48.206 --> 00:30:49.827
It's not your boss's fault that you

00:30:49.827 --> 00:30:51.792
can't do what you want,
it's not your parents' fault

00:30:51.792 --> 00:30:53.455
or your wife or husband's fault.

00:30:53.455 --> 00:30:54.845
It's not your kids fault,
it's not your friend's fault.

00:30:54.845 --> 00:30:56.825
It's nobody's fault, it's your fault.

00:30:56.825 --> 00:30:58.644
You're not doing the
thing that you want to do,

00:30:58.644 --> 00:31:00.415
it's nobody else's fault but yourself.

00:31:00.415 --> 00:31:03.473
Own it, accept it and
start making some changes.

00:31:03.473 --> 00:31:06.748
As soon as you feel like
you're being pulled somewhere,

00:31:06.748 --> 00:31:08.815
that you want to go try this thing out.

00:31:08.815 --> 00:31:10.998
That it's calling to you, then you need

00:31:10.998 --> 00:31:15.417
to make an adjustment in your
schedule to allow for it.

00:31:15.417 --> 00:31:17.015
Even if it's a temporary thing,

00:31:17.015 --> 00:31:18.446
maybe it's to learn salsa dancing.

00:31:18.446 --> 00:31:19.994
Maybe you go and you have a great time

00:31:19.994 --> 00:31:21.659
at that first class and
you want to keep doin' it.

00:31:21.659 --> 00:31:22.492
Maybe you take that first class

00:31:22.492 --> 00:31:24.094
and you say, you know
what, that's not for me,

00:31:24.094 --> 00:31:26.062
and you pull back, that's okay.

00:31:26.062 --> 00:31:27.841
What's not okay is the regret.

00:31:27.841 --> 00:31:29.550
What's not okay is continuing to think

00:31:29.550 --> 00:31:31.025
of this idea that you
have, continue to wish

00:31:31.025 --> 00:31:33.274
you had more time to spend on this thing

00:31:33.274 --> 00:31:36.046
that's way over here,
and you stay stuck here.

00:31:36.046 --> 00:31:36.879
Because until you find out,

00:31:36.879 --> 00:31:38.805
you're going to constantly live in regret.

00:31:38.805 --> 00:31:41.201
And it's going to get worse,
and worse, and worse, and worse.

00:31:41.201 --> 00:31:44.030
The more that you want
this, and you're stuck here

00:31:44.030 --> 00:31:45.325
it's going to get worse.

00:31:45.325 --> 00:31:46.856
You're going to get increasingly unhappy.

00:31:46.856 --> 00:31:50.527
And so for me, it's not
about getting so unhappy

00:31:50.527 --> 00:31:52.979
that you have to make this huge change,

00:31:52.979 --> 00:31:56.146
it's constantly adjusting what you do.

00:31:57.062 --> 00:31:58.634
Constantly adjusting your priorities,

00:31:58.634 --> 00:32:00.663
constantly adjusting your schedule.

00:32:00.663 --> 00:32:02.257
And I strongly encourage you guys to

00:32:02.257 --> 00:32:04.361
whenever you feel like
something is out of whack,

00:32:04.361 --> 00:32:06.206
on the business side,
on the personal side,

00:32:06.206 --> 00:32:07.546
on the development side, whatever it is.

00:32:07.546 --> 00:32:08.814
You feel like you're being pulled

00:32:08.814 --> 00:32:11.910
to do something else other than
what you're doing right now,

00:32:11.910 --> 00:32:16.573
find a time to adjust your
schedule and make it happen.

00:32:16.573 --> 00:32:17.461
It's on you to do it.

00:32:17.461 --> 00:32:18.512
Nobody's coming to save you.

00:32:18.512 --> 00:32:20.865
This is your responsibility,
to live your life,

00:32:20.865 --> 00:32:22.674
to be the best version of you.

00:32:22.674 --> 00:32:25.332
And that happens when you
follow that intuition.

00:32:25.332 --> 00:32:28.102
And you find out, because
finding out and getting

00:32:28.102 --> 00:32:30.080
the no, and getting a failure,

00:32:30.080 --> 00:32:32.204
and getting you know
understand that's not for you.

00:32:32.204 --> 00:32:35.919
Finding out is way better
than never finding out.

00:32:35.919 --> 00:32:39.105
Finding out and losing is way
better than never finding out.

00:32:39.105 --> 00:32:39.938
So do it.

